    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        700,
        520
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        420
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Audio: Load Video's audio goes straight into Video Combine.\niPhone clips (.mov) can also carry an 'apac' spatial-audio track that many ffmpeg builds can't decode, which makes Video Combine fail. In that case connect 'iPhone clips: first audio track only' -> Video Combine 'audio' instead (pick the same video in it); it decodes only track 0:a:0.\n\nsmooth 0.6 = the script's temporal smoothing. fixed_dots on = no flicker. even_size keeps H.264 happy. Long/large clips: set frame_load_cap for previews; all frames are held in RAM.\n\nDepthDots tips\n- Faces: model large, res 1036, detail 1.5, shade 0.3 (Enhance).\n- More/denser dots: raise dots; gamma >1 pushes dots to close areas; floor = background density.\n- color_mode: depth_shaded (tone = depth), flat (solid ink), source_color (needs source_image).\n- dark = white dots on black. size_by_depth = closer dots bigger.\n- Have a depth map already? LoadImage -> DepthDots Depth From Image -> Enhance/Render (see depth_map_in workflow).\n- The SaveImage filename_prefix comes from the Render node: <prefix>_<model>_r<res>_n<dots>_g.._s.._x..[_det.._sh..][_fixed][_dark][_color]..."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
